msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/sized.md:23
msgid ""
"Motivation: Being able to specify between types whose size are known and "
"compile time and types whose size are known at runtime is useful for"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/sized.md:26
msgid ""
"The Sized trait is automatically implemented by types with a known size at "
"compile-time."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/sized.md:29
msgid ""
"This trait is also automatically added to any type parameter that doesn't "
"opt-out of being sized."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/sized.md:32
msgid "Most types implement `Sized`: they have a compile-time known size."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/sized.md:34
msgid ""
"Types like `[T]`, `str` and `dyn Trait` are all dynamically sized types. "
"Their size is stored as part of the reference to the value of that type."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/sized.md:37
msgid "Type parameters automatically implement `Sized` unless specified."
msgstr ""

